Hi Ed,

I wanted to send one more update regarding this issue. I decided to simplify the model and only include 2 factors (instead of 3). For this two-factor model, the correlation/covariance is estimated fine (at .9) with the default prior settings, initial values, and using JAGS. So it seems like this issue only occurs when multiple correlations are estimated with these priors + JAGS.

Thanks for all the input you've given me about this issue. If anything, I learned a lot about blavaan, JAGS, and Bayes. :)

Sonja

